-/** Shared OkHttpClient instance reused across all downloads. */
-private val sharedHttpClient = OkHttpClient()
+/**
+ * Shared OkHttpClient instance reused across all downloads.
+ *
+ * Built through React Native's `OkHttpClientProvider.createClient()` so it picks up
+ * any custom `OkHttpClientFactory` the app installed — for Wavio that is the
+ * ssl-trust module's factory, which carries the SSLSocketFactory backing
+ * self-signed / private-CA TOFU trust and mTLS client certs. A bare
+ * `OkHttpClient()` uses only the system trust store, so downloads from such a
+ * server fail the handshake with `CertPathValidatorException: Trust anchor for
+ * certification path not found` even though streaming and browsing work.
+ *
+ * `createClient()` — NOT `createClientBuilder()`: only the former consults the
+ * factory (the latter returns a plain builder, and is what the sibling
+ * FileSystemDownloadTask used, which is why it had the same bug).
+ *
+ * Timeouts are set explicitly because `createClient()` inherits RN's 0ms
+ * (infinite) defaults, whereas the bare client this replaces had OkHttp's 10s.
+ * Without them a stalled download would hang forever.
+ */
+private val sharedHttpClient = OkHttpClientProvider.createClient()
+  .newBuilder()
+  .connectTimeout(30, TimeUnit.SECONDS)
+  .readTimeout(60, TimeUnit.SECONDS)
+  .writeTimeout(60, TimeUnit.SECONDS)
+  .build()
 
